S4: Stanford Stratified Structure Solver (http://fan.group.stanford.edu/S4/)

A program for computing electromagnetic fields in periodic, layered
structures, developed by Victor Liu (victorliu@alumni.stanford.edu) of the
Fan group in the Stanford Electrical Engineering Department.

## Documentation

- Markdown overview: `doc/index.md` (and sibling `doc/*.md`)
- Upstream Sphinx sources: `doc/source/*.rst` (historical; Makefile/Lua/Python install paths)
- Legacy HTML snapshot: `docold/index.html` (not maintained)

There is **no** `doc/index.html` in this tree unless you build Sphinx yourself.

## simulation_core integration (this fork)

Parent `simulation_core` builds S4 via CMake (`add_subdirectory(3rdparty/S4)`):

- Always builds **`S4_bridge`** (C API in `S4/s4_bridge.h`) and links it into `simulation`.
- Full static **`S4`** library and S4 tests build only when parent enables MKL
  (`-DCMAKE_ENABLE_MKL=ON` / `build_simulation.py --mkl on`).
- Default eigen backend: `S4_EIGEN_BACKEND=MEKIL` (uses `infrastructure::uca`).

Stable surface for parent code: **`s4_bridge_*`** + `include/layer/s4_bridge_adapt.hpp`,
not the Lua/Python front-ends described in upstream docs.

Build from `simulation_core`:

```bash
source scripts/init-simulation-build-env.sh build
python3 scripts/build_simulation.py --mkl on   # full S4 + bridge
```

RCWA baseline (Lua, not CI): parent `scripts/build_install_s4_lua.sh` builds `S4lua`
linked to MEKIL `libS4`. Optional legacy Python path `scripts/build_install_s4_python.sh`
is unmaintained — do not confuse with `S4_bridge` or `S4lua`.

Upstream install/dev notes in `doc/source/install.rst` remain historical.
